On http://mw.lojban.org/papri/Lojban it says:

   - Lojban is unambiguous in syntax. Natural languages often have
   ambiguous sentences =E2=80=94 does "He's left" mean that he's still here=
 or that
   he's gone? Lojban systematically eliminates this.


=E2=80=8B"He's left" is unambiguous. It means he is no longer there. =E2=80=
=8BTherefore
this is a really bad example, since it doesn't illustrate the point.
Nothing comes to mind that might have been meant instead.

=E2=80=8Bstevo=E2=80=8B


